'''Asteroida''' (as-tẹ-roi′dä̤), ''n. pl.'' [NL., < Gr. ἀστεροειδής, star-like: see ''asteroid.''] '''1.''' In Gegenbaur’s system of classification, a class of echinoderms, the sea-stars or starfishes, consisting of the orders ''Asterida, Brisingida, Ophiurida,'' and ''Euryalida.''—'''2.''' Same as ''Alcyonaria.''

'''asteroidal''' (as-tẹ-roi′dal), ''a.'' [< ''asteroid'' (or ''Asteroida'') + ''-al.''] '''1.''' Resembling a star.—'''2.''' Pertaining to the asteroids.—'''3.''' Pertaining to the starfishes.—'''4.''' Same as ''alcyonarian.''

