'''Asterolepis''' (as-te̤-rol′e-pis), ''n.'' [NL., < Gr. ἀστήρ, a star, + λεπίς, a scale.] A genus of gigantic primitive fishes, now found only in a fossil state in the Old Red Sandstone. {{smaller|From their remains it would seem that these fishes must sometimes have attained the length of 18 or 20 feet.}}
